a.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D],\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D\\in V\">\\([\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D],\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Category}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Category}_S\\)</span> (category predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"a87b7e1119b63b2c\" href=\"?note=a87b7e1119b63b2c\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-category.md\">../batch04/58-df-category.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Functor}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Functor}_S\\)</span> (functor predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"877f1061e295cf5f\" href=\"?note=877f1061e295cf5f\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-functor.md\">../batch18/58-df-functor.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NaturalTransformation}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{NaturalTransformation}_S\\)</span> (natural-transformation predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"970e2b8779070da0\" href=\"?note=970e2b8779070da0\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-natural-transformation.md\">../batch09/58-df-natural-transformation.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Obj},\\operatorname{Mor}\">\\(\\operatorname{Obj},\\operatorname{Mor}\\)</span> (designated category accessors)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcCat2FunctorCategory}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcCat2FunctorCategory}_S\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}cat2\\text{-}functor\\text{-}category} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcCat2FunctorCategory}_S([\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D],\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Category}_S(\\mathcal C)\\land\\mathrm{Category}_S(\\mathcal D)\\land\\mathrm{Category}_S([\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D])\\land\\operatorname{Obj}([\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D])=\\{F\\mid\\mathrm{Functor}_S(F,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D)\\}\\land\\operatorname{Mor}([\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D])=\\{(F,G,\\eta)\\mid F,G\\in\\operatorname{Obj}([\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D])\\land\\mathrm{NaturalTransformation}_S(\\eta,F,G,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D)\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}cat2\\text{-}functor\\text{-}category} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcCat2FunctorCategory}_S([\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D],\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Category}_S(\\mathcal C)\\land\\mathrm{Category}_S(\\mathcal D)\\land\\mathrm{Category}_S([\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D])\\land\\operatorname{Obj}([\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D])=\\{F\\mid\\mathrm{Functor}_S(F,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D)\\}\\land\\operatorname{Mor}([\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D])=\\{(F,G,\\eta)\\mid F,G\\in\\operatorname{Obj}([\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D])\\land\\mathrm{NaturalTransformation}_S(\\eta,F,G,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D)\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Requiring <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D]\">\\([\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D]\\)</span> itself to satisfy the category axioms closes the former gap that specified only two carrier sets and omitted identities and composition.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-ax-zfc]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch04/58-df-category.md","status":"resolved","id":"a87b7e1119b63b2c","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch04/58-df-category.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-func